---
title: Suspicious Data Loader-Style Connected App Authorization
id: 8f1c1a2e-4b3d-4e7a-9c2f-1a2b3c4d5e01
status: experimental
description: Detects authorization of a new connected app in Salesforce resembling the legitimate Data Loader tool, matching UNC6040's initial access vector.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/unc6040-proactive-hardening-recommendations
    - https://thehackernews.com/2025/06/google-exposes-vishing-group-unc6040.html
tags:
    - attack.initial_access
    - attack.t1528
    - attack.t1566.004
logsource:
    category: application
    product: salesforce
    service: setup_audit_trail
detection:
    selection:
        Action: 'ConnectedApp Authorization'
        AppName|contains:
            - 'Data Loader'
            - 'Dataloader'
    filter_known_good:
        AppName: 'Salesforce Data Loader'
    condition: selection and not filter_known_good
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate ISV or admin-approved integration named similarly to Data Loader
level: high

---
title: OAuth Device Code Grant Shortly After Unsolicited Support Contact
id: 8f1c1a2e-4b3d-4e7a-9c2f-1a2b3c4d5e02
status: experimental
description: Detects OAuth Device Flow authorization events, which UNC6040 abuses by talking a victim through entering an attacker-supplied device code.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/technical-analysis-vishing-threats/
tags:
    - attack.initial_access
    - attack.t1528
    - attack.t1566.004
logsource:
    category: application
    product: salesforce
    service: login_history
detection:
    selection:
        LoginType: 'OAuth-Device-Flow'
        Status: 'Success'
    condition: selection
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate device-flow logins from CLI tools, IoT integrations, or CI systems
level: medium

---
title: Incremental Bulk Export Resembling Sync Activity from Newly Authorized App
id: 8f1c1a2e-4b3d-4e7a-9c2f-1a2b3c4d5e03
status: experimental
description: Detects a pattern of repeated small-to-moderate volume API/bulk data pulls from a connected app authorized within the prior 24 hours, matching UNC6040's slow exfiltration behavior designed to evade bulk-export alerting.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/unc6040-proactive-hardening-recommendations
tags:
    - attack.exfiltration
    - attack.collection
    - attack.t1530
logsource:
    category: application
    product: salesforce
    service: event_monitoring
detection:
    selection:
        EventType:
            - 'API'
            - 'BulkApiRequest'
            - 'ReportExport'
    timeframe: 24h
    condition: selection | count(RequestId) by AppName, UserId > 10
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate high-frequency integration or ETL sync recently reauthorized
level: medium

